# Code owners for the CoreWeave skills library.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
# ------------------------------------
# Listing a path here auto-requests review from its owner. That is ALL it does.
# It does not *require* that review until a ruleset turns on "Require review
# from Code Owners" for `main` — see docs/RELEASING.md, "Repo-admin actions".
# This file is step one of two; without step two it is a routing hint.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT A CATCH-ALL
# ----------------------------
# There is no `*` line. Ordinary skill edits keep whatever review flow they
# have today. Only the surfaces where an unreviewed change reaches a
# customer's cluster are owned here — a catch-all would bury those in the
# noise of every prose tweak, which is how a CODEOWNERS file stops being read.

# --- Pinned dependencies ----------------------------------------------------
# These hold the commit SHA, chart versions, and release pin that decide which
# remote code runs under the customer's own credentials. Reviewing a bump means
# reading the UPSTREAM diff, not the changed pin line: see CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Pinned dependencies".
/_snippets/coreweave-cks.md                                    @coreweave/docs
/skills/cw-self-managed-inference/body.md                      @coreweave/docs
/skills/cw-load-model-to-bucket/references/s3-client-setup.md  @coreweave/docs

# The automation that proposes those bumps. Loosen a regex here and the pins
# silently stop being proposed — no error, just nothing.
/.github/renovate.json5                                        @coreweave/docs

# --- The gates themselves ---------------------------------------------------
# Whatever can switch a check off is owned alongside the check. Both scripts
# are stdlib-only and run in build.yml.
/.github/workflows/                                            @coreweave/docs
/scripts/check_pinned_deps.py                                  @coreweave/docs
/scripts/lint_skill_content.py                                 @coreweave/docs
